1
00:00:02,966 --> 00:00:07,532
The jungles of Yunnan,
southern China.

2
00:00:09,199 --> 00:00:14,199
Life here is more surprising,
brighter and more bizarre

3
00:00:14,199 --> 00:00:17,699
than almost anywhere
in the country.

4
00:00:17,699 --> 00:00:21,199
Each species holds
extraordinary skills

5
00:00:21,199 --> 00:00:24,199
to harvest
the jungle's bounty.

6
00:00:32,199 --> 00:00:36,699
This is just one of many
diverse landscapes.

7
00:00:36,699 --> 00:00:40,166
Full of rare
and surprising creatures.

8
00:00:42,565 --> 00:00:46,065
For the first time,
we'll uncover

9
00:00:46,065 --> 00:00:49,065
their remarkable untold stories...

10
00:00:53,065 --> 00:00:56,565
In The Hidden Kingdoms of China.

11
00:01:11,065 --> 00:01:14,400
This handsome devil
is the Asian hornbill.

12
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:20,433
And he's a family man.

13
00:01:20,433 --> 00:01:23,433
For the next four months,

14
00:01:23,433 --> 00:01:28,433
this super dad
will be the sole provider

15
00:01:28,433 --> 00:01:31,433
for his family of three.

16
00:01:40,699 --> 00:01:42,199
Mom's not lazy.

17
00:01:42,199 --> 00:01:44,199
When it comes to parenting,

18
00:01:44,199 --> 00:01:47,699
she is just as dedicated
as dad.

19
00:01:50,866 --> 00:01:55,866
She enters her nest
before laying her eggs,

20
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:58,866
shedding her own flight feathers,

21
00:01:58,866 --> 00:02:01,366
rendering her totally entombed.

22
00:02:01,366 --> 00:02:05,366
Welcome to motherhood,
Asian hornbill style.

23
00:02:05,366 --> 00:02:08,366
With dad often away hunting,

24
00:02:08,366 --> 00:02:11,366
she needs this extreme measure

25
00:02:11,366 --> 00:02:16,366
to hide her growing chicks
from nest raiders.

26
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:25,233
Hornbills bond for life.

27
00:02:25,233 --> 00:02:28,733
Our pair is nesting
in this tree

28
00:02:28,733 --> 00:02:31,500
for the tenth year straight.

29
00:02:34,999 --> 00:02:38,499
Mom's only outlet
to the world

30
00:02:38,499 --> 00:02:44,499
is a slit half an inch wide
in the tree hollow.

31
00:02:44,499 --> 00:02:48,499
Wide enough for dad
to supply food

32
00:02:48,499 --> 00:02:53,499
and narrow enough to keep
nest-raiding predators out.

33
00:03:01,565 --> 00:03:06,065
Dad returns to the nest
multiple times a day.

34
00:03:06,065 --> 00:03:09,565
He can deliver over
100 pieces of fruit

35
00:03:09,565 --> 00:03:12,065
to his family each visit.

36
00:03:12,065 --> 00:03:15,565
He stores the fruit
in a special pouch

37
00:03:15,565 --> 00:03:18,065
at the base of his neck.

38
00:03:18,065 --> 00:03:21,065
To pass the fruit onto mom,

39
00:03:21,065 --> 00:03:23,565
he skillfully rolls each one

40
00:03:23,565 --> 00:03:27,065
to the tip of his huge beak.

41
00:03:27,065 --> 00:03:30,065
100 Feet up
from the jungle floor,

42
00:03:30,065 --> 00:03:35,565
it's a mouth-to-mouth
precision operation, most of the time.

43
00:03:43,599 --> 00:03:48,099
He's under intense pressure
to feed hungry mouths.

44
00:03:58,333 --> 00:04:02,100
Sugary fruit alone
will not sustain his young.

45
00:04:04,999 --> 00:04:08,000
Dad has to up his game.

46
00:04:10,598 --> 00:04:14,598
A tiny owl chick,
a protein hit.

47
00:04:14,598 --> 00:04:16,598
But then...

48
00:04:16,598 --> 00:04:22,598
The meal falls all the way
to the jungle floor.

49
00:04:22,598 --> 00:04:26,598
Retrieving it is too risky.

50
00:04:35,366 --> 00:04:39,866
Dad has no choice
but to hunt again.

51
00:04:47,999 --> 00:04:50,100
Mom waits anxiously.

52
00:04:53,433 --> 00:04:55,933
He returns with a bigger chick.

53
00:05:00,166 --> 00:05:04,166
A prize he can't afford to lose.

54
00:05:32,532 --> 00:05:36,532
He crushes the bones
and tries again.

55
00:05:42,766 --> 00:05:44,766
Too big!

56
00:05:50,766 --> 00:05:54,766
But he's not giving up.

57
00:06:02,065 --> 00:06:05,233
Success at last.

58
00:06:07,599 --> 00:06:10,099
Thanks to super parents,
the chicks

59
00:06:10,099 --> 00:06:12,467
will soon be ready to fledge.

60
00:06:16,965 --> 00:06:19,965
It's not just our hornbills;

61
00:06:19,965 --> 00:06:24,465
all creatures here
show ingenious adaptations

62
00:06:24,465 --> 00:06:27,465
to this hidden kingdom.

63
00:06:31,465 --> 00:06:35,465
But the jungle needs the animals

64
00:06:35,465 --> 00:06:40,465
as much as the animals
need the jungle.

65
00:06:47,632 --> 00:06:49,632
The Asian elephant.

66
00:06:49,632 --> 00:06:52,632
Numbering only 300 in China,

67
00:06:52,632 --> 00:06:54,632
they are elusive.

68
00:06:57,632 --> 00:07:00,632
These gardeners of the jungle

69
00:07:00,632 --> 00:07:03,632
help maintain
this hidden kingdom.

70
00:07:18,299 --> 00:07:21,299
They have a huge appetite,

71
00:07:21,299 --> 00:07:27,299
spending up to 18 hours a day
just eating.

72
00:07:27,299 --> 00:07:32,299
These elephants devour
hundreds of pounds of plants.

73
00:07:32,299 --> 00:07:35,799
They're not exactly
fussy eaters.

74
00:07:38,799 --> 00:07:42,299
Just one part of the process

75
00:07:42,299 --> 00:07:45,033
helping to preserve
a healthy jungle.

76
00:07:49,666 --> 00:07:52,866
♪ ♪

77
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:58,900
Every time the herd moves on,

78
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:02,400
the elephants deposit
undigested seeds,

79
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:06,400
which pass through
their stomachs intact.

80
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:13,900
Piles of dung
scattered far and wide

81
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:18,900
through the jungle make
the perfect dispersal system

82
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:20,400
for vegetation.

83
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:24,400
Many trees here rely on animals

84
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,400
to spread their seeds.

85
00:08:34,666 --> 00:08:37,166
And trees provide clean air,

86
00:08:37,166 --> 00:08:40,632
shelter and food
to all who live here.

87
00:08:44,699 --> 00:08:48,199
They are magnificent
silent heroes.

88
00:08:48,199 --> 00:08:52,699
And yet we know few
of their stories.

89
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:58,699
This one is said to be
the largest banyan tree

90
00:08:58,699 --> 00:09:01,199
in all of China;

91
00:09:01,199 --> 00:09:04,199
a venerable 300 years old.

92
00:09:08,199 --> 00:09:13,199
Out of its branches
thousands of aerial roots

93
00:09:13,199 --> 00:09:15,699
spread in all directions.

94
00:09:15,699 --> 00:09:18,199
From these, others sprout,

95
00:09:18,199 --> 00:09:20,699
reaching for the ground,

96
00:09:20,699 --> 00:09:24,199
thickening and forming
new trunks.

97
00:09:27,632 --> 00:09:32,132
The crown covers
an astonishing 88,000 square feet,

98
00:09:32,132 --> 00:09:36,632
the size of one and a half
American football fields.

99
00:09:38,966 --> 00:09:41,966
This banyan is so big

100
00:09:41,966 --> 00:09:45,966
that it's its own
one-tree forest.

101
00:09:57,832 --> 00:09:59,832
Regarded as sacred,

102
00:09:59,832 --> 00:10:04,832
people leave red banners
and lanterns as offerings,

103
00:10:04,832 --> 00:10:09,699
in the belief they bring
happiness and good luck.

104
00:10:21,599 --> 00:10:25,599
Covering an area
larger than California,

105
00:10:25,599 --> 00:10:29,599
Yunnan is a unique part of China.

106
00:10:29,599 --> 00:10:35,099
Home to over half
the entire country's plant species.

107
00:10:35,099 --> 00:10:38,066
And yet, the jungles
shouldn't be here.

108
00:10:41,199 --> 00:10:43,699
Mountains border the jungles,

109
00:10:43,699 --> 00:10:47,632
keeping out the cold air
of winter heading south.

110
00:10:49,933 --> 00:10:55,433
Deep, narrow valleys
funnel in warm, wet air,

111
00:10:55,433 --> 00:11:01,433
making it one of the most northern
jungles in the world.

112
00:11:08,732 --> 00:11:12,232
A secret realm
full of wildlife stories

113
00:11:12,232 --> 00:11:15,699
about to be revealed
for the first time.

114
00:11:21,999 --> 00:11:27,499
Mysterious animals hide
in remote corners of this kingdom.

115
00:11:27,499 --> 00:11:31,499
Camera traps in China's
Yunnan jungle

116
00:11:31,499 --> 00:11:33,499
capture surprising creatures.

117
00:11:33,499 --> 00:11:36,499
A pair of marbled cats.

118
00:11:36,499 --> 00:11:41,499
Footage of them in China
is extremely rare.

119
00:11:41,499 --> 00:11:46,499
These shy creatures are
one of the least known

120
00:11:46,499 --> 00:11:49,599
of the small wild cats.

121
00:11:52,732 --> 00:11:58,232
Jungles make up less than 7%
of the Earth's surface,

122
00:11:58,232 --> 00:12:01,732
yet are home to half
the world's

123
00:12:01,732 --> 00:12:04,166
land-based plants and animals.

124
00:12:06,665 --> 00:12:12,665
The perfect combination of light,
water, nutrients, and terrain

125
00:12:12,665 --> 00:12:17,165
creates diversity
found nowhere else in China.

126
00:12:17,165 --> 00:12:20,165
Life here should be easy.

127
00:12:27,165 --> 00:12:31,165
Competition for these resources
is fierce,

128
00:12:31,165 --> 00:12:37,165
so every animal adopts
its own clever survival strategy,

129
00:12:37,165 --> 00:12:43,165
allowing a host of creatures
to live side by side.

130
00:12:48,299 --> 00:12:50,299
From feathered friends......

131
00:12:50,299 --> 00:12:52,299
To creepy crawlies,

132
00:12:52,299 --> 00:12:55,299
mud-sucking butterflies
to honeybees,

133
00:12:55,299 --> 00:12:59,299
the world's only
venomous primate......

134
00:12:59,299 --> 00:13:04,299
To one of the largest
tree-living mammals

135
00:13:04,299 --> 00:13:06,299
on the planet,

136
00:13:06,299 --> 00:13:11,299
all have one thing
in common:

137
00:13:11,299 --> 00:13:15,299
they've found ways to adapt

138
00:13:15,299 --> 00:13:18,299
to this jungle environment.

139
00:13:18,299 --> 00:13:22,299
A place where leaves
and branches

140
00:13:22,299 --> 00:13:25,299
harbor the unimaginable.

141
00:13:29,565 --> 00:13:34,565
In Yunnan, some of the coolest
creatures

142
00:13:34,565 --> 00:13:39,065
are filmed here
for the first time.

143
00:13:48,798 --> 00:13:52,298
With names that sound
like characters

144
00:13:52,298 --> 00:13:55,298
plucked out of a comic book,

145
00:13:55,298 --> 00:13:58,298
caterpillars are
marvels of nature.

146
00:13:58,298 --> 00:14:00,798
This is Checkers,
named after

147
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:03,666
its geometric pattern
down its back.

148
00:14:05,632 --> 00:14:11,300
Shaped like a shield,
this is, well, the Shield.

149
00:14:14,433 --> 00:14:18,433
With a colored, nut-looking lump
in his middle,

150
00:14:18,433 --> 00:14:20,333
this is Almondback.

151
00:14:22,299 --> 00:14:26,333
And dressed to impress,
the Jester.

152
00:14:28,565 --> 00:14:33,933
They're little known and many
are still undescribed by science.

153
00:14:37,032 --> 00:14:42,532
Like high-vis vests,
bright colors are a warning sign

154
00:14:42,532 --> 00:14:46,532
which predators need
to avoid at all costs.

155
00:14:46,532 --> 00:14:49,532
Imitation, chemical weapons
and camouflage

156
00:14:49,532 --> 00:14:54,032
are all tools
in the arsenal of survival

157
00:14:54,032 --> 00:14:56,966
for these jungle caterpillars.

158
00:14:59,266 --> 00:15:02,266
Thousands of nails
cover Pin Cushion.

159
00:15:02,266 --> 00:15:05,766
The pink spots mounted
on his rear

160
00:15:05,766 --> 00:15:07,766
consist of minute pins

161
00:15:07,766 --> 00:15:10,766
that he inflates
when threatened,

162
00:15:10,766 --> 00:15:14,333
to attack any predator
that crosses his path.

163
00:15:16,899 --> 00:15:19,899
Dragon Head emerges
from the egg

164
00:15:19,899 --> 00:15:22,399
with his horns complete,

165
00:15:22,399 --> 00:15:26,399
ready to defend himself;
six in total.

166
00:15:26,399 --> 00:15:29,399
The long, arching
outer pairs

167
00:15:29,399 --> 00:15:32,399
lead to a central pointy crown

168
00:15:32,399 --> 00:15:34,500
fit for a Chinese dragon.

169
00:15:38,133 --> 00:15:41,133
Snake Head wears a mask,

170
00:15:41,133 --> 00:15:43,633
complete with painted eyes.

171
00:15:43,633 --> 00:15:47,633
All that airborne predators
are seeing

172
00:15:47,633 --> 00:15:50,133
is a dangerous snake.

173
00:15:50,133 --> 00:15:55,133
He can happily carry on
and feed.

174
00:16:02,133 --> 00:16:06,633
But there's one
that predators truly fear...

175
00:16:06,633 --> 00:16:08,133
Medusa.

176
00:16:16,066 --> 00:16:19,066
Medusa is locked and loaded

177
00:16:19,066 --> 00:16:23,066
with a halo
of stinging spines.

178
00:16:23,066 --> 00:16:27,066
For her, it's all about defense.

179
00:16:27,066 --> 00:16:31,066
Each razor-sharp spike
is a hollow needle

180
00:16:31,066 --> 00:16:34,066
connected to a poison gland.

181
00:16:34,066 --> 00:16:37,066
She's ready to inject a toxin

182
00:16:37,066 --> 00:16:40,266
into any unlucky predator
that comes too close.

183
00:16:45,698 --> 00:16:50,698
Those that don't use weapons
rely on camouflage,

184
00:16:50,698 --> 00:16:53,198
like the twig caterpillar.

185
00:16:53,198 --> 00:16:55,698
Legs set far apart,

186
00:16:55,698 --> 00:17:00,198
he creates a characteristic loop
as he walks.

187
00:17:05,198 --> 00:17:09,198
He can also make
like a statue,

188
00:17:09,198 --> 00:17:13,333
remaining motionless
and undetected for days.

189
00:17:17,232 --> 00:17:20,232
Others protect themselves
by building

190
00:17:20,232 --> 00:17:24,232
some of the most intricate
constructions

191
00:17:24,232 --> 00:17:26,232
in the animal kingdom.

192
00:17:26,232 --> 00:17:31,232
Inside these leaves,
stuck together by her own silk,

193
00:17:31,232 --> 00:17:34,599
is a living caterpillar
known as Witch's Hat.

194
00:17:36,865 --> 00:17:39,365
To accommodate a growing body,

195
00:17:39,365 --> 00:17:43,365
she adds to her hat,
leaf by leaf.

196
00:17:43,365 --> 00:17:45,365
When she's an adult,

197
00:17:45,365 --> 00:17:48,365
she'll become a wingless moth

198
00:17:48,365 --> 00:17:54,365
full of eggs waiting
for a male to fertilize them.

199
00:17:54,365 --> 00:17:56,599
This is her home for life.

200
00:17:59,133 --> 00:18:03,200
She's even worked out
a way to discard her waste.

201
00:18:06,333 --> 00:18:11,333
She gently balances her droppings
on tiny silk threads,

202
00:18:11,333 --> 00:18:16,333
ready to jettison them
as far as she can.

203
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:25,333
All these caterpillars
have the need to eat

204
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:27,833
and not be eaten.

205
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:31,333
Stunning looks
and impressive adaptations

206
00:18:31,333 --> 00:18:33,833
go a long way.

207
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:38,333
After hours of roaming
these jungle hillsides,

208
00:18:38,333 --> 00:18:41,333
our herd is still eating.

209
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:49,333
Even in the heat of the day,

210
00:18:49,333 --> 00:18:54,333
the elephants are geared up
for keeping cool.

211
00:18:54,333 --> 00:18:57,333
They have few sweat glands,

212
00:18:57,333 --> 00:19:02,333
but are equipped
with their own air-conditioning system.

213
00:19:02,333 --> 00:19:05,333
Hair keeps most mammals warm,

214
00:19:05,333 --> 00:19:09,333
but for these elephants
it does the opposite.

215
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:15,200
When hair covers the skin,

216
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:18,200
it acts as an insulator.

217
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:21,700
When sparse,
it dissipates heat,

218
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:25,200
cooling the bodies
of the herd

219
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:28,200
up to an extra 20%.

220
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:31,700
Stinging insects
have no problems

221
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,200
getting through the hair.

222
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:36,700
Elephants are thick-skinned,

223
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:40,200
but more sensitive
than they look.

224
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:43,200
The herd feels every bite.

225
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:48,700
Flapping ears help,
but there is a better solution.

226
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:52,200
They spray themselves with dust

227
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:57,200
to keep annoying insects
and parasite numbers down.

228
00:20:03,199 --> 00:20:07,199
It also acts
as elephant sunscreen.

229
00:20:07,199 --> 00:20:12,199
And besides,
dust bathing is just fun.

230
00:20:20,199 --> 00:20:26,199
Any excuse for this youngster
to roll in the dirt.

231
00:20:41,565 --> 00:20:47,033
When the fun is over, the herd
needs to head somewhere special.

232
00:20:48,799 --> 00:20:54,799
A tricky journey to the bottom
of the valley lies ahead.

233
00:21:02,265 --> 00:21:06,765
The herd has mastered
a system

234
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:11,467
which stops them careering down
the slippery slopes.

235
00:21:16,032 --> 00:21:19,532
Placing all weight
on their front feet,

236
00:21:19,532 --> 00:21:22,666
they bend their hind legs
to slow them down.

237
00:21:25,598 --> 00:21:28,098
Not exactly mountain goats,

238
00:21:28,098 --> 00:21:33,098
but more than capable
of tackling the steep terrain.

239
00:21:33,098 --> 00:21:35,598
This is their destination.

240
00:21:40,598 --> 00:21:45,098
Where the river slows,
mineral-rich sediment settles.

241
00:21:45,098 --> 00:21:47,098
The elephant's gold.

242
00:21:51,098 --> 00:21:55,098
Salt and nutrients
concentrate right here,

243
00:21:55,098 --> 00:21:58,098
and our elephants know it.

244
00:22:02,732 --> 00:22:05,732
The herd has the knowledge
and the tools

245
00:22:05,732 --> 00:22:07,766
to access what it needs.

246
00:22:12,866 --> 00:22:18,866
The elephants dig up potassium,
sodium and phosphorus-rich salts,

247
00:22:18,866 --> 00:22:22,366
essential for maintaining
muscle function.

248
00:22:28,399 --> 00:22:31,399
Their trunks alone are made up

249
00:22:31,399 --> 00:22:34,666
of 150,000 bundles
of muscle fibers.

250
00:22:37,832 --> 00:22:41,799
Helping them to suck up gallons
of this life-giving water.

251
00:22:44,499 --> 00:22:49,499
But elephants aren't the only
mineral diggers around here.

252
00:22:49,499 --> 00:22:53,033
Someone else is watching
their every step.

253
00:22:59,965 --> 00:23:04,965
Jungle jade follows
in the footsteps of the elephant herd.

254
00:23:13,699 --> 00:23:18,699
A swallowtail, named after
those swallow-like forked hind wings.

255
00:23:22,367 --> 00:23:26,367
Butterflies often gather
at the river's edge,

256
00:23:26,367 --> 00:23:30,367
in a behavior
known as mud puddling.

257
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:33,367
It's exactly what you think.

258
00:23:33,367 --> 00:23:38,100
Still water
in the elephant's footprints is ideal.

259
00:23:41,433 --> 00:23:46,333
Little is known about mud puddling,
but we do know some things.

260
00:23:54,765 --> 00:24:00,265
Most of the butterflies found
around the puddles are males,

261
00:24:00,265 --> 00:24:03,766
and scientists believe
they're after the salts.

262
00:24:05,866 --> 00:24:11,366
He uses a long, hollow tube
that's part of his mouth

263
00:24:11,366 --> 00:24:13,366
to extract precious nutrients,

264
00:24:13,366 --> 00:24:17,733
which he will pass on
to his partner during mating.

265
00:24:21,632 --> 00:24:24,599
The rest he expels.

266
00:24:28,466 --> 00:24:33,166
This boost of nutrients improves
the viability of the female's eggs,

267
00:24:33,166 --> 00:24:35,466
increasing the couple's chances

268
00:24:35,466 --> 00:24:38,933
of passing on their genes
to the next generation.

269
00:24:47,065 --> 00:24:49,565
Some young in these jungles

270
00:24:49,565 --> 00:24:52,133
get a different kind
of parental gift.

271
00:24:54,266 --> 00:24:57,266
A male crested treeswift.

272
00:24:57,266 --> 00:25:02,266
An exposed branch
offers an easy takeoff,

273
00:25:02,266 --> 00:25:07,266
but here he also hides
an extraordinary nest.

274
00:25:11,166 --> 00:25:15,366
It's just one and a half
inches wide

275
00:25:15,366 --> 00:25:18,699
and a perfect fit
for one precious egg.

276
00:25:21,732 --> 00:25:26,732
The next three weeks
are dad's most important,

277
00:25:26,732 --> 00:25:31,732
because in this nest
is his only chick,

278
00:25:31,732 --> 00:25:34,732
just a few days old.

279
00:25:34,732 --> 00:25:39,732
So vulnerable,
she should never be left alone

280
00:25:39,732 --> 00:25:43,232
until she can fly the nest.

281
00:25:48,232 --> 00:25:51,732
Her survival is all
about teamwork.

282
00:25:51,732 --> 00:25:54,232
Dad needs his partner.

283
00:25:54,232 --> 00:25:57,232
While one is nest-sitting,

284
00:25:57,232 --> 00:26:00,232
the other is airborne.

285
00:26:03,999 --> 00:26:07,699
Hunting insects to feed
their growing chick.

286
00:26:10,100 --> 00:26:15,600
From a special pouch
in the back of her throat,

287
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:21,100
mom regurgitates a food ball
containing hundreds of insects,

288
00:26:21,100 --> 00:26:25,600
hoping to satisfy
her chick's constant appetite.

289
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:32,600
Through thick and thin,

290
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:37,100
mom and dad continuously
swap duties......

291
00:26:37,100 --> 00:26:42,100
No matter what the jungle weather
throws at them.

292
00:26:44,799 --> 00:26:50,799
As the rain begins to fall,
mom takes the first shift.

293
00:26:57,599 --> 00:27:03,166
The conditions become more severe,
leaving dad with the baby.

294
00:27:21,366 --> 00:27:24,366
Spreading out
his breast feathers,

295
00:27:24,366 --> 00:27:28,366
he does his best
to shelter her.

296
00:27:36,366 --> 00:27:42,366
Neither mom nor dad have
successfully hunted during the rain.

297
00:27:42,366 --> 00:27:48,366
Wet weather means there are
fewer flying insects to catch.

298
00:27:52,366 --> 00:27:58,366
Once the sky is clear,
both parents must find food.

299
00:28:01,132 --> 00:28:07,433
Abandoning the nest
leaves our chick alone and defenseless.

300
00:28:15,999 --> 00:28:20,499
Mom and dad have no choice
but to hunt

301
00:28:20,499 --> 00:28:24,999
at the same time,
leaving their chick exposed.

302
00:28:24,999 --> 00:28:28,499
Instinct tells her
to stay absolutely still.

303
00:28:28,499 --> 00:28:31,999
If she does,
her incredible camouflage

304
00:28:31,999 --> 00:28:36,333
might just be enough
to keep her alive.

305
00:28:39,166 --> 00:28:45,166
As soon as mom returns,
our chick feels safe to move again.

306
00:28:54,799 --> 00:29:00,799
She has survived the first tests
on her journey to independence.

307
00:29:05,799 --> 00:29:08,799
It's a proud parent moment.

308
00:29:22,999 --> 00:29:25,499
The jungle never sleeps.

309
00:29:25,499 --> 00:29:27,999
Hunters stalk the night.

310
00:29:27,999 --> 00:29:30,999
They must use the darkness

311
00:29:30,999 --> 00:29:34,499
to get the food they need.

312
00:29:34,499 --> 00:29:36,999
The clock is ticking.

313
00:29:39,999 --> 00:29:43,499
A slow loris,
known in China

314
00:29:43,499 --> 00:29:46,699
as the bee monkey.

315
00:29:48,632 --> 00:29:52,632
The world's only
venomous primate......

316
00:29:56,632 --> 00:30:00,632
With a bite that may
protect them

317
00:30:00,632 --> 00:30:02,632
against predators.

318
00:30:10,132 --> 00:30:14,132
The slow loris has evolved
special blood vessels

319
00:30:14,132 --> 00:30:16,632
in his wrists and ankles,

320
00:30:16,632 --> 00:30:19,132
delivering oxygen
to the muscles,

321
00:30:19,132 --> 00:30:23,632
allowing him to hold on
for hours at a time.

322
00:30:23,632 --> 00:30:27,132
But he's not made
for hanging around.

323
00:30:27,132 --> 00:30:30,799
The loris is a night expert.

324
00:30:34,099 --> 00:30:38,099
Forward-facing eyes give him
stereoscopic vision

325
00:30:38,099 --> 00:30:40,599
for pinpoint depth perception,

326
00:30:40,599 --> 00:30:44,599
and a reflective layer
behind his retina

327
00:30:44,599 --> 00:30:47,599
delivers brilliant
low-light images,

328
00:30:47,599 --> 00:30:51,099
essential for being
a nocturnal predator.

329
00:30:51,099 --> 00:30:53,099
Insects are cold-blooded,

330
00:30:53,099 --> 00:30:58,099
so in the cool of the night
they slow down,

331
00:30:58,099 --> 00:31:01,099
playing right into the hands...

332
00:31:01,099 --> 00:31:03,599
Of the slow loris.

333
00:31:03,599 --> 00:31:06,599
It's more stealth than speed.

334
00:31:11,300 --> 00:31:13,300
Few escape.

335
00:31:20,300 --> 00:31:23,300
Tonight, though,
he's distracted...

336
00:31:23,300 --> 00:31:25,300
By her.

337
00:31:34,332 --> 00:31:40,332
But she's not in heat
and would rather have a bite herself.

338
00:31:52,566 --> 00:31:56,566
She's giving him
the cold shoulder.

339
00:31:56,566 --> 00:31:59,066
No luck this time.

340
00:32:08,233 --> 00:32:12,233
There is a faster
night hunter here,

341
00:32:12,233 --> 00:32:14,733
using a different strategy.

342
00:32:14,733 --> 00:32:16,733
A fishing bat.

343
00:32:16,733 --> 00:32:19,733
He relies not on eyesight,

344
00:32:19,733 --> 00:32:21,733
but on sound.

345
00:32:21,733 --> 00:32:26,733
His high-frequency clicks
bounce back off the water,

346
00:32:26,733 --> 00:32:29,233
helping to echolocate prey.

347
00:32:33,233 --> 00:32:36,733
He can distinguish
between insects

348
00:32:36,733 --> 00:32:38,733
that rest stock-still...

349
00:32:38,733 --> 00:32:43,233
And fish that create
a moving target

350
00:32:43,233 --> 00:32:47,233
when their ripples
break the surface.

351
00:32:51,099 --> 00:32:57,099
With hook-like claws,
he's well equipped to catch fish,

352
00:32:57,099 --> 00:33:01,099
which make up over half
his diet.

353
00:33:05,966 --> 00:33:10,466
A ripple on the surface
reveals the target.

354
00:33:10,466 --> 00:33:15,466
The fishing bat is
in full hunting mode.

355
00:33:20,466 --> 00:33:22,466
He misses.

356
00:33:28,299 --> 00:33:30,299
He circles back.

357
00:33:30,299 --> 00:33:35,299
This time he locks on
to the prey...

358
00:33:35,299 --> 00:33:39,299
And then returns
to the roost

359
00:33:39,299 --> 00:33:41,799
to devour his catch.

360
00:33:51,999 --> 00:33:57,499
Whether hunter or hunted,
raising a family or finding food,

361
00:33:57,499 --> 00:34:01,100
adaptation is key
to surviving the jungle.

362
00:34:04,166 --> 00:34:09,166
Phayre's leaf monkeys spend
almost all their time

363
00:34:09,166 --> 00:34:13,666
in the canopy doing
what they do best...

364
00:34:13,666 --> 00:34:15,666
Eating leaves.

365
00:34:30,266 --> 00:34:33,766
They seldom come down
from the trees,

366
00:34:33,766 --> 00:34:38,000
so when they do,
it's a privileged view.

367
00:34:40,366 --> 00:34:46,366
These rare monkeys are given
the highest protection in China.

368
00:34:46,366 --> 00:34:52,866
And a recent discovery of a much
larger group than normal,

369
00:34:52,866 --> 00:34:55,366
200 strong, is encouraging.

370
00:34:55,366 --> 00:34:59,866
This troop is venturing
into the open

371
00:34:59,866 --> 00:35:03,366
in search of a special treat.

372
00:35:10,799 --> 00:35:15,799
When conditions come together
in the perfect mix,

373
00:35:15,799 --> 00:35:18,799
the leaf monkeys do something

374
00:35:18,799 --> 00:35:23,299
that has never been filmed
in Yunnan before.

375
00:35:28,899 --> 00:35:31,899
Clouds build and boil,

376
00:35:31,899 --> 00:35:35,899
pushed up by the warm air......

377
00:35:40,899 --> 00:35:44,399
Until they reach bursting point.

378
00:35:44,399 --> 00:35:50,399
The rainy season lasts
five months of the year.

379
00:35:58,565 --> 00:36:02,065
The downpour gives birth
to waterfalls

380
00:36:02,065 --> 00:36:04,766
cascading for more than 100 feet.

381
00:36:17,399 --> 00:36:20,399
This water encourages the growth

382
00:36:20,399 --> 00:36:24,399
of mosses, grasses
and other plants.

383
00:36:24,399 --> 00:36:27,399
Rich pickings for our monkeys.

384
00:36:31,266 --> 00:36:35,766
The waterfall is
in this troop's territory,

385
00:36:35,766 --> 00:36:41,266
but they only visit
for one type of plant

386
00:36:41,266 --> 00:36:44,266
when the conditions are perfect.

387
00:36:44,266 --> 00:36:47,266
Today is the day.

388
00:36:51,899 --> 00:36:56,899
100 Feet up
on the wet, sheer rock face,

389
00:36:56,899 --> 00:36:58,899
they feast.

390
00:36:58,899 --> 00:37:01,899
It may just be moss,

391
00:37:01,899 --> 00:37:05,899
but our monkeys are eating
the unusual.

392
00:37:05,899 --> 00:37:09,899
Few herbivores
have a taste for it

393
00:37:09,899 --> 00:37:12,899
because it's so
nutritionally poor.

394
00:37:18,899 --> 00:37:23,899
Exactly what the benefits are
remain a mystery,

395
00:37:23,899 --> 00:37:26,899
but our troop's behavior shows

396
00:37:26,899 --> 00:37:29,899
how adaptable they can be

397
00:37:29,899 --> 00:37:31,899
in this jungle.

398
00:37:39,866 --> 00:37:42,366
Having had their fill,

399
00:37:42,366 --> 00:37:45,866
it's time for a quick drink

400
00:37:45,866 --> 00:37:50,866
before the troop turns
its back to the sun

401
00:37:50,866 --> 00:37:52,866
to dry off.

402
00:37:57,866 --> 00:38:01,866
Time to return
to the treetops

403
00:38:01,866 --> 00:38:03,866
where they belong.

404
00:38:03,866 --> 00:38:07,366
Below the canopy
in a clearing,

405
00:38:07,366 --> 00:38:10,366
an Asiatic black bear.

406
00:38:14,999 --> 00:38:17,499
At over 250 pounds,

407
00:38:17,499 --> 00:38:21,999
his diet consists mainly
of fruit and nuts.

408
00:38:21,999 --> 00:38:24,499
To satisfy his appetite,

409
00:38:24,499 --> 00:38:28,499
he spends much of his day
foraging.

410
00:38:28,499 --> 00:38:34,499
But when our hungry bear
takes a break from eating,

411
00:38:38,499 --> 00:38:42,499
what better way
to spend the time

412
00:38:42,499 --> 00:38:45,499
than to just frolic?

413
00:39:00,333 --> 00:39:05,333
Then, something in the air
grabs his attention.

414
00:39:05,333 --> 00:39:08,333
His eyesight isn't the best.

415
00:39:08,333 --> 00:39:12,333
He relies instead
on his other senses.

416
00:39:12,333 --> 00:39:15,333
He's hearing and smelling bees.

417
00:39:15,333 --> 00:39:19,333
Yunnan is home
to two thirds

418
00:39:19,333 --> 00:39:21,833
of China's honeybee species.

419
00:39:25,833 --> 00:39:28,833
Each one helps to maintain

420
00:39:28,833 --> 00:39:31,833
the area's impressive
plant diversity.

421
00:39:40,166 --> 00:39:43,666
Using her long straw-like tongue
called a proboscis,

422
00:39:43,666 --> 00:39:47,166
she sucks the nectar
out of the flower,

423
00:39:47,166 --> 00:39:50,766
storing it in her honey stomach
for the journey home.

424
00:39:57,333 --> 00:40:02,899
Asian honeybees live in enclosed
cavities, including tree hollows.

425
00:40:05,698 --> 00:40:09,899
Colonies can be 34,000 strong.

426
00:40:13,366 --> 00:40:15,866
Honeybees are superorganisms.

427
00:40:15,866 --> 00:40:20,366
Life in here is about
working together

428
00:40:20,366 --> 00:40:22,866
for the greater good.

429
00:40:22,866 --> 00:40:27,100
Their nest is
an architectural wonder.

430
00:40:28,832 --> 00:40:33,332
The bees build aerial cities
of multiple combs,

431
00:40:33,332 --> 00:40:35,566
arranged parallel
to one another.

432
00:40:37,899 --> 00:40:41,399
A mass of hexagonal cells,

433
00:40:41,399 --> 00:40:46,899
home to the bees' larvae,
pollen and honey.

434
00:40:46,899 --> 00:40:50,899
There are plenty
of bee colonies,

435
00:40:50,899 --> 00:40:55,399
but this tree
has the bear's attention.

436
00:40:55,399 --> 00:40:58,399
Honey drips down the trunk

437
00:40:58,399 --> 00:41:00,899
from an abandoned hive

438
00:41:00,899 --> 00:41:03,399
and tastes wonderful.

439
00:41:03,399 --> 00:41:07,399
A favorite jungle snack
of his.

440
00:41:14,932 --> 00:41:18,932
Within relatively easy reach.

441
00:41:18,932 --> 00:41:22,932
No chance of getting stung.

442
00:41:28,565 --> 00:41:31,565
And he wants more......

443
00:41:31,565 --> 00:41:33,565
Much more.

444
00:41:33,565 --> 00:41:39,065
These bears spend half
of their life in trees.

445
00:41:39,065 --> 00:41:45,065
They're one of the largest
arboreal mammals on the planet.

446
00:41:45,065 --> 00:41:50,566
His strong legs and forearms
make short work of the climb.

447
00:41:54,333 --> 00:41:59,333
While he takes care of the honey.

448
00:42:08,532 --> 00:42:12,532
With a full stomach,
getting down

449
00:42:12,532 --> 00:42:17,032
is a lot trickier
than getting up.

450
00:42:21,565 --> 00:42:26,565
Getting down is not a problem
for our herd.

451
00:42:30,732 --> 00:42:33,732
Arriving again
at their watering hole,

452
00:42:33,732 --> 00:42:36,232
elephants help maintain
this kingdom,

453
00:42:36,232 --> 00:42:38,732
and people, too,
are taking steps

454
00:42:38,732 --> 00:42:41,732
to preserve the stunning array
of plants

455
00:42:41,732 --> 00:42:43,933
and animals
of Yunnan's jungles.

456
00:42:47,665 --> 00:42:52,665
Numbering only 170 individuals
in the early 1990s,

457
00:42:52,665 --> 00:42:56,400
this elephant population
has almost doubled.

458
00:43:00,032 --> 00:43:04,532
Today, this guy is hope
for the future.

459
00:43:04,532 --> 00:43:08,133
He's just a few weeks old.

460
00:43:12,033 --> 00:43:17,533
Completely reliant on mom
for the next 18 months,

461
00:43:17,533 --> 00:43:22,033
he will develop a close bond
with her

462
00:43:22,033 --> 00:43:25,799
until he's about 8 years old.

463
00:43:31,500 --> 00:43:35,500
There is a lot to learn.

464
00:43:38,500 --> 00:43:41,500
Not drowning, for one.

465
00:43:49,865 --> 00:43:53,865
His life story lies ahead.

466
00:43:58,865 --> 00:44:02,865
Many more will be discovered

467
00:44:02,865 --> 00:44:06,865
in China's hidden jungle kingdom.

